      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Considering your soil pH is 6.2, bone meal is a better option than blood meal. Bone meal is less acidic and tends to be safer for low-pH soils, while blood meal can be too alkaline and harsh for acidic soils. However, it's also worth noting that a 3-4 week time frame may not be sufficient for compost to fully nutrientize the soil, so you might need to supplement with bone meal.",
